# FIGHTO - Act I dialogue (missions 1-5). Format: speaker: line

@m01_home_arrive
damian: Police tape. Scorch marks up to the second floor.
damian: Three years I dreamed about walking through that door. Now there's no door.
damian: Eli was supposed to be here. He'd have been sitting on the porch, pretending he wasn't waiting.

@m01_home_search
damian: Mom's piano. Melted.
damian: The fire started inside, not at the wiring. Somebody poured something on these floors.
damian: That's not an accident. That's a message.
damian: Eli kept a notebook for everything. If it survived, it's in the back room.

@m01_notebook
damian: His notebook. Half of it's ash.
damian: "Night shift, Halberd Shipping, Pier 9. Crate 4471 is warm. Crates aren't supposed to be warm."
damian: "Told M. about it. He said forget it." M... Marcus.

@m01_cop
cop: Damian Cross. Heard you were out. Didn't figure you'd come back here.
damian: It's my house, Dunn. What's left of it.
cop: Fire marshal says faulty wiring. Case closed.
damian: And my brother?
cop: Nineteen-year-old kid takes off after his house burns down. Happens every week in The Blocks.
cop: Do yourself a favor. Don't go asking questions on my streets.

@m01_marcus
marcus: Look at this. Damian Cross, back from the dead. Sit down, sit down.
damian: Where's Eli, Marcus?
marcus: Straight to it. Okay. I don't know. That's the truth.
marcus: He was working nights at Halberd Shipping, down in Ironworks. Good money, no questions asked.
marcus: Then three weeks ago, your house goes up, and he's just... gone. No call. Nothing.
damian: His notebook says he told you about a warm crate.
marcus: He said a lot of things. Kid was paranoid. I told him to keep his head down.
marcus: Look, you've got no money and no place to sleep. I've got both.
marcus: There's an apartment on the west side of The Blocks. It's yours. Keys, a bed, a TV that mostly works.
marcus: And when you're ready, I've got work. Real money. Help me, and I'll help you look for him.
damian: You always did know how to make a deal sound like a favor.
marcus: That's because it is one, brother.

@m01_safehouse
damian: Four walls and a lock. Better than a cell.
damian: Somebody burned my home and took my brother, and everybody in this city wants me to forget it.
damian: Not happening, Eli. I'm going to find you.

@m02_brief
marcus: First job. Easy one.
marcus: Tommy Kowalski runs the Suds City Laundromat, two blocks south. He owes me eight hundred.
marcus: He's late three times. He's starting to think I'm a charity.
damian: And if he doesn't have it?
marcus: Tommy always has it. He just needs to be reminded. Gently, if possible.
marcus: He drinks with the Kings, though. If his friends get involved, don't be gentle.

@m02_tommy
tommy: Oh no. No no no. Damian Cross? They let you out?
damian: Marcus says you owe him eight hundred, Tommy.
tommy: I - look, business is slow, the machines keep breaking -
damian: You're wearing a new watch.
tommy: Hey guys? GUYS! A little help out here!

@m02_caught
tommy: Okay! Okay! Don't hit me!
tommy: I got three hundred on me. That's it, that's everything, I swear on my mother.
damian: That watch says otherwise.
tommy: It was a gift! From my mother! Who I swore on!

@m02_spare
damian: Give me the three hundred. Keep the watch.
tommy: You serious? You're - thank you. Thank you, Damian.
damian: Pay Marcus the rest by Friday. And Tommy - you hear anything about my brother, you call me.
tommy: Eli? Yeah. Yeah, I will. I swear.

@m02_beat
damian: Marcus told me to remind you. I'm going to make sure you remember.
tommy: Damian, come on, we went to school together!

@m02_beat_after
tommy: Take it! Take the watch, take everything!
damian: Pleasure doing business, Tommy.
thug: The Kings are gonna hear about this, Cross.

@m02_report_spared
marcus: Three hundred. And Tommy's still got his watch, I hear.
damian: He'll pay the rest. People pay when they still have something to lose.
marcus: Huh. Prison made you soft or smart. I'll let you know which.
marcus: Keep the cut. There's a man at the Fight Pit in Ironworks who saw Eli a few weeks ago.

@m02_report_beat
marcus: Eight hundred and a Swiss watch. And half the Kings now want your head.
damian: You said not to be gentle.
marcus: I said if his friends got involved. Relax. It's good for business when people are scared of you.
marcus: Keep the cut. There's a man at the Fight Pit in Ironworks who saw Eli a few weeks ago.

@m03_signup
sal: Fresh face. Big shoulders. Prison posture. You fight?
damian: I'm looking for somebody. Brick Halloran.
sal: Everybody's looking for Brick. Brick only talks to people who can stand up to him.
sal: You want an audience, you climb the ladder. Three rounds. Survive and you meet the champ.
sal: Rules are simple: no guns, no knives, no crying. Get in the ring.

@m03_round2
announcer: The new guy stays standing! Pay the man!
sal: Not bad. Now let's see how you do when they come in pairs.
sal: Keep your guard up. Two men means two directions to get hit from.

@m03_brick
announcer: Ladies and gentlemen, the undefeated king of the Ironworks, "BRICK" HALLORAN!
sal: Brick's never been knocked down. Watch his big swings - block them, or dodge them.
sal: Your stamina's your life in there. Run dry and he'll put you through the floor.

@m03_win
announcer: HE DID IT! BRICK HALLORAN IS DOWN! WE HAVE A NEW CHAMPION!
sal: Kid, you just made me a lot of money. Come back any time. The Pit Ladder's open for you.

@m03_brick_talk
brick: Nobody's put me down in six years. Who are you?
damian: Damian Cross. You saw my brother. Eli.
brick: The skinny kid with the notebook. Yeah. He came in a month ago asking questions.
brick: About Halberd Shipping. About the crates that come in at night and leave in black vans.
brick: I told him what I tell everybody: those crates belong to Nikolai Varga. And Varga's buyers aren't from around here.
brick: That kid was scared, Cross. But he kept asking anyway. Takes guts.

@m04_brief
marcus: Here's the job. A buyer in Ironworks wants one specific car.
marcus: Black Vortex GT, sitting in the lot at Silverline Motors in West Hills. Two grand for twenty minutes of work.
damian: Who's the buyer?
marcus: Does it matter?
damian: Brick says Eli was asking about Varga. So yes, it matters.
marcus: ...It's Varga. Fine. Meet him, get paid, ask him whatever you want. Just deliver the car first.
marcus: And take this. West Hills has private security, and the Kings have been watching that car.

@m04_phone
marcus: Damian! Who did you take that car from?
damian: A car lot. Like you told me.
marcus: That car belongs to the Kings' boss. He parked it at Silverline as a favor to the owner.
marcus: The Kings think you stole from them. Get to Varga's before they find you.

@m04_varga
varga: So you are the man who stole a king's crown. Nikolai Varga.
varga: Your Marcus sends me a car. You send the Kings a declaration of war. I like it.
damian: I didn't come for your approval. My brother, Eli. He was asking about you.
varga: Eli Cross. Yes. A good kid. Bad timing.
varga: He worked at Halberd, where my special shipments come in. He looked inside a crate he should not have.
varga: Then he started asking where my crates go. And three days later, men in black came to the docks.
varga: Not police. Not federal. They do not wear badges, and they do not miss.
damian: Where are the crates going?
varga: Tomorrow night, one more crate arrives at Halberd. My buyer pays more than for all the cars in this city.
varga: Help me take it, and I'll tell you everything I know about the men in black.

@m05_brief
varga: Halberd Shipping, Pier 9. Container 4471 came in this morning.
damian: 4471. That number was in my brother's notebook.
varga: Then it is fate. Dmitri and Lev will go with you. They are good boys - they mostly shoot the right people.
varga: Take the shotgun. Halberd hired new security this month. They are not friendly.

@m05_inside
damian: This isn't a shipping warehouse. Look at the power lines.
damian: Somebody built a lab in here. A cheap one, in a hurry.

@m05_pods
damian: Tanks. Glowing tanks. What the hell is Varga selling?
damian: Eli was right. Crates aren't supposed to be warm.

@m05_shard
shard: ...
damian: It's... a stone? No. Metal. It's warm. It's humming.
damian: Wait - it's getting brighter. Like it knows me.
shard: ...cross... damian... cross...
damian: Did it just say my name?

